// Hello, slang
//
// Slang is a small scripting language in the family of Lua: tables for
// everything, functions as values, coroutines. Its parser is written in
// slang and can be extended by your programs, so the language grows new
// syntax as a library.
//
// Every page of this tour is a program you can edit and run. Press Run
// (or Ctrl+Enter), change something, run it again.
print("Hello, slang!\n")

local name = "world"
print("Hello, ", name, "\n")
